00:27:54.162 --> 00:27:59.284
would have liked to break with family tradition and do a different job than that of his ancestors.

00:28:03.884 --> 00:28:06.246
But the war put an end to his dream.

00:28:07.326 --> 00:28:09.386
It's a bit of a job.

00:28:10.126 --> 00:28:10.926
I am a rapper.

00:28:11.946 --> 00:28:13.147
These are traditional reports.

00:28:15.104 --> 00:28:15.403
Samba,

00:28:15.483 --> 00:28:16.605
34 years old,

00:28:17.086 --> 00:28:18.267
has been rapping since he was 16.

00:28:19.288 --> 00:28:20.169
Before 2016,

00:28:20.328 --> 00:28:22.810
He gave concerts in front of hundreds of people.

00:28:23.672 --> 00:28:24.071
Today,

00:28:24.112 --> 00:28:24.833
his only audience,

00:28:25.634 --> 00:28:26.795
some young people from the neighborhood.

00:28:28.036 --> 00:28:29.297
Since then, the war has returned,

00:28:29.356 --> 00:28:30.577
I couldn't do a concert.

00:28:31.318 --> 00:28:31.898
We were scared,

00:28:32.700 --> 00:28:34.080
because there are threats.

00:28:35.863 --> 00:28:37.243
We can organize a concert,

00:28:38.525 --> 00:28:41.126
The bad guys can come in and attack us.

00:28:55.730 --> 00:28:56.491
In these words,

00:28:57.192 --> 00:29:02.019
Samba is worried because the war against the jihadists is turning into an ethnic conflict.

00:29:20.511 --> 00:29:20.811
Samba

00:29:20.852 --> 00:29:21.372
is Fulani,

00:29:22.272 --> 00:29:29.296
An ethnic group present in 15 West African countries and traditionally very involved in butchery and livestock farming.

00:29:31.147 --> 00:29:31.567
Today,

00:29:31.607 --> 00:29:33.929
The people are caught between the jihadists,

00:29:34.409 --> 00:29:36.730
the military and farmers.

00:29:38.671 --> 00:29:40.632
Most of the people are semi-nomadic.

00:29:41.352 --> 00:29:42.653
At the beginning of the dry season,

00:29:43.393 --> 00:29:45.954
They migrate with their herds to the southern pastures.

00:29:46.894 --> 00:29:47.795
But since the war,

00:29:48.455 --> 00:29:51.237
The state no longer manages livestock transhumance corridors.

00:29:52.457 --> 00:29:52.938
Result,

00:29:53.478 --> 00:29:55.318
the oxen destroy part of the crops,

00:29:55.759 --> 00:29:58.579
triggering conflicts between farmers and herdsmen.

00:29:59.607 --> 00:30:02.170
When animals go down without superego,

00:30:02.210 --> 00:30:04.691
There are also disputes over fields.

00:30:05.070 --> 00:30:05.730
So, all the time,

00:30:05.750 --> 00:30:06.412
These are conflicts.

00:30:06.852 --> 00:30:08.153
For some time now,

00:30:08.913 --> 00:30:12.634
The skins were under a lot of pressure from the administration.

00:30:13.015 --> 00:30:13.816
And we take you,

00:30:14.236 --> 00:30:14.816
we lock you up.

00:30:15.596 --> 00:30:17.518
And the breeder has a schedule to be locked up.

00:30:18.478 --> 00:30:19.979
So instead of being locked up,

00:30:20.058 --> 00:30:23.020
he prefers to pay the million to get out.

00:30:23.840 --> 00:30:24.261
Indeed,

00:30:24.262 --> 00:30:25.261
Malian justice,

00:30:25.321 --> 00:30:26.083
often corrupt,

00:30:26.563 --> 00:30:28.364
makes them pay astronomical fines.

00:30:29.392 --> 00:30:30.192
This resentment,

00:30:30.752 --> 00:30:33.996
a Fulani exploited it to rally his fellow men to the jihadist cause.

00:30:35.537 --> 00:30:35.977
This man,

00:30:36.397 --> 00:30:37.278
This is Amadou Koufa.

00:30:38.239 --> 00:30:38.980
To seduce them,

00:30:39.480 --> 00:30:41.541
he named his group Katiba du Massina,

00:30:42.261 --> 00:30:49.048
A reference to this golden age, when the Fulani caliphate of Massina dominated central Mali in the 19th century.

00:30:52.388 --> 00:31:05.051
I take this opportunity to thank God for allowing me to see the day when thousands of Fulani joined the jihadists to fight in the path of God until martyrdom.

00:31:08.512 --> 00:31:11.953
Amadou Koufa began his career as a preacher in the 1990s.

00:31:12.755 --> 00:31:16.155
The audio cassettes of his sermons were a hit among the Fulani.

00:31:21.508 --> 00:31:22.167
It's in Mopti,

00:31:22.888 --> 00:31:25.509
the capital of the region where he recorded his sermons,

00:31:25.971 --> 00:31:27.431
in the studios of Radio, Sagan,

00:31:27.991 --> 00:31:29.413
the most listened to in the area.

00:31:37.176 --> 00:31:38.498
Today a radio host,

00:31:39.198 --> 00:31:44.980
Ousmane Koïta was the jihadist leader's sound engineer.

00:31:50.163 --> 00:31:54.007
We stopped these cassettes in the market.

00:31:54.287 --> 00:31:59.951
They are rarely found nowadays, because almost all the hunters of these tapes have been arrested. Once,

00:32:00.030 --> 00:32:00.351
twice.

00:32:02.172 --> 00:32:05.894
Before Amadou Koufa became an outlaw in 2012,

00:32:05.913 --> 00:32:08.836
Ousmane recorded his sermons every week for three years.

00:32:10.497 --> 00:32:11.817
He remembers one of them,

00:32:12.397 --> 00:32:13.798
particularly explicit.

00:32:15.380 --> 00:32:16.740
You who are marginalized,

00:32:16.780 --> 00:32:23.823
you who are really robbed, feet and bothered by the wearer of Malian uniform,

00:32:24.303 --> 00:32:25.942
You will no longer be taxed or given information,

00:32:26.202 --> 00:32:27.304
nor other taxes,

00:32:27.344 --> 00:32:27.864
absolutely nothing.

00:32:28.423 --> 00:32:28.983
Come with me.

00:32:30.305 --> 00:32:33.645
Words that hit the mark at the time.

00:32:33.705 --> 00:32:37.707
It is true that the malicious insistence had annoyed the population.

00:32:38.807 --> 00:32:39.047
A lot,

00:32:39.247 --> 00:32:39.508
a lot,

00:32:39.548 --> 00:32:40.248
a lot of ink.

00:32:41.107 --> 00:32:45.829
They immediately followed his call and left.

00:32:45.830 --> 00:32:47.371
With the influx of new recruits,

00:32:48.151 --> 00:32:51.471
Amadou Koufa's group has increased its influence over central Mali.

00:32:53.512 --> 00:32:57.434
Mopti is located at the confluence of the Niger and Bani rivers,

00:32:58.775 --> 00:33:03.636
A strategic location for river trade between the North and the South of Mali.

00:33:05.417 --> 00:33:06.438
Since 2019,

00:33:07.259 --> 00:33:10.740
only the river separates Mopti from the areas controlled by the jihadists.

00:33:12.291 --> 00:33:14.433
If the exchanges between the two banks have not stopped,

00:33:15.294 --> 00:33:15.795
in front,

00:33:16.515 --> 00:33:17.836
Sharia law applies.

00:33:19.397 --> 00:33:20.699
When they cross the river,

00:33:21.538 --> 00:33:24.020
women must now wear the black hijab,

00:33:24.701 --> 00:33:25.923
at the risk of being beaten.

00:33:27.084 --> 00:33:27.624
The thieves,

00:33:27.683 --> 00:33:27.804
them,

00:33:28.585 --> 00:33:31.086
expose themselves to having their hands and feet cut off.

00:33:37.971 --> 00:33:42.213
Four repentant jihadists who lived on the other side of the river agreed to meet us.

00:33:43.054 --> 00:33:48.076
All are Fulani and say they joined the ranks of the Islamists because they were persecuted.

00:33:48.855 --> 00:33:54.097
This former shepherd even saw his village attacked by the Malian army and ozo hunters.

00:33:56.138 --> 00:33:59.759
They say that all Fulani are jihadists, but that is not the case.

00:34:00.951 --> 00:34:02.192
So they attack our villages,

00:34:02.614 --> 00:34:03.273
kill women,

00:34:04.055 --> 00:34:07.076
2 or 3 year old grandchildren who are unable to defend themselves.

00:34:07.738 --> 00:34:12.202
And even old women who don't know how to handle a rifle.

00:34:12.641 --> 00:34:13.463
And during the attacks,

00:34:13.463 --> 00:34:14.963
you have parents who were killed.

00:34:16.686 --> 00:34:16.806
Yes.

00:34:18.487 --> 00:34:19.307
Once enlisted,

00:34:19.987 --> 00:34:23.130
Those who want to fight must buy their own weapons and motorcycles.

00:34:23.871 --> 00:34:26.693
Some have spent up to 1,800 euros to equip themselves.

00:34:28.155 --> 00:34:29.076
Everyone participates.

00:34:29.300 --> 00:34:30.360
To camp life, nomad.

00:34:33.902 --> 00:34:34.043
Me,

00:34:34.603 --> 00:34:35.583
during these three years,

00:34:37.806 --> 00:34:39.907
I went out fighting almost all the time.

00:34:43.170 --> 00:34:44.251
But since I am a shepherd,

00:34:44.590 --> 00:34:45.851
I also took care of animals.

00:34:47.753 --> 00:34:48.713
So when I was going to fight,

00:34:48.934 --> 00:34:50.735
someone replaced me to leather the animals.

00:34:53.177 --> 00:34:54.157
There were many cows,

00:34:54.838 --> 00:34:56.858
often more than 1,500 head of cattle.

00:34:58.460 --> 00:34:59.141
Sometimes, more,

00:34:59.561 --> 00:35:00.121
sometimes less.

00:35:03.083 --> 00:35:03.885
Among these animals,

00:35:04.105 --> 00:35:06.007
There were also those that we had taken from our enemies.

00:35:09.570 --> 00:35:11.831
Those who go to war are entitled to their share of the spoils.

00:35:12.552 --> 00:35:14.215
But the emir takes 60% of it

00:35:14.335 --> 00:35:16.195
to finance the operations of the Katiba.

00:35:18.619 --> 00:35:19.739
For this ex-fighter,

00:35:20.340 --> 00:35:21.681
This distribution is unfair.

00:35:22.501 --> 00:35:23.822
And he lets his boss know.

00:35:25.621 --> 00:35:26.280
Before coming,

00:35:26.740 --> 00:35:28.782
I was not satisfied with the justice of the whites,

00:35:29.344 --> 00:35:30.844
And I am no more so with you.

00:35:31.744 --> 00:35:32.266
So now,

00:35:32.326 --> 00:35:33.067
let me go.

00:35:33.626 --> 00:35:33.867
Like that,

00:35:33.867 --> 00:35:35.208
you can do as you see fit.

00:35:36.849 --> 00:35:38.791
But the main reason for their departure,

00:35:39.130 --> 00:35:40.813
It is the austere lifestyle imposed.

00:35:41.333 --> 00:35:44.396
Jihadists apply a Salafist interpretation of the Quran.

00:35:45.536 --> 00:35:46.958
I couldn't do what I wanted.

00:35:47.617 --> 00:35:49.018
I was afraid to say what I thought.

00:35:49.739 --> 00:35:50.521
Because if I did,

00:35:50.521 --> 00:35:51.842
I was called a hypocritical Muslim.

00:35:52.501 --> 00:35:54.324
All of this was part of their application of Sharia law.

00:35:57.072 --> 00:35:59.012
Everything you do must be validated by them.

00:36:00.494 --> 00:36:01.793
Even if it doesn't suit you,

00:36:01.934 --> 00:36:02.614
you have to do it.

00:36:05.396 --> 00:36:06.356
Whether you like it or not,

00:36:06.635 --> 00:36:07.376
They indoctrinate you.

00:36:09.077 --> 00:36:09.456
Above all,

00:36:09.697 --> 00:36:11.557
They were told to change the way they pray.

00:36:12.137 --> 00:36:14.077
They force you to put your hands like this to pray.

00:36:15.579 --> 00:36:17.420
Were you asked to become a Salafist?

00:36:18.400 --> 00:36:18.519
Yes.

00:36:19.780 --> 00:36:19.920
Me,

00:36:20.059 --> 00:36:20.820
I am malevolent.

00:36:21.221 --> 00:36:22.141
They wanted to change that,

00:36:22.481 --> 00:36:23.382
but I didn't agree,

00:36:23.422 --> 00:36:24.322
so I left the group.

00:36:26.762 --> 00:36:28.403
Practiced here for centuries,

00:36:28.824 --> 00:36:31.244
Malequism advocates a tolerant reading of the Koran,

00:36:31.664 --> 00:36:32.844
unlike Salafism,

00:36:33.385 --> 00:36:35.106
imported to Mali in the 1980s,

00:36:35.666 --> 00:36:36.746
by preachers,

00:36:37.086 --> 00:36:38.427
originating from the Gulf countries.

00:36:39.367 --> 00:36:42.429
Disappointed at not having found the just society they imagined,

00:36:43.130 --> 00:36:44.489
all returned to their village,

00:36:45.130 --> 00:36:46.411
with their former neighbors,

00:36:47.050 --> 00:36:48.371
often of different ethnicities.

00:36:51.405 --> 00:36:52.686
When I returned home,

00:36:52.945 --> 00:36:54.106
when the Dogons saw me,

00:36:54.126 --> 00:36:54.487
at first,

00:36:54.606 --> 00:36:55.367
They were afraid of me.

00:36:57.648 --> 00:36:58.449
But after some time,

00:36:58.568 --> 00:37:00.170
Those I live with were no longer afraid.

00:37:01.030 --> 00:37:02.791
They look at me now as if I had done nothing,

00:37:03.351 --> 00:37:04.532
and that they had nothing to reproach me for.

00:37:05.932 --> 00:37:06.873
They got used to me.

00:37:09.233 --> 00:37:11.775
The Fulani and the Dogon will always need each other.

00:37:14.568 --> 00:37:15.130
For example,

00:37:15.309 --> 00:37:16.331
to cultivate fields,

00:37:16.411 --> 00:37:17.192
build houses,

00:37:17.711 --> 00:37:18.333
dig wells,

00:37:18.333 --> 00:37:19.653
The Dogons do it best.

00:37:21.735 --> 00:37:22.856
For animal breeding,

00:37:22.996 --> 00:37:23.918
The Fulani are more gifted.

00:37:26.960 --> 00:37:27.661
Persecuted,

00:37:28.061 --> 00:37:29.643
notably by Malian soldiers,

00:37:30.222 --> 00:37:33.085
Hundreds of thousands of Fulani have left central Mali.

00:37:33.827 --> 00:37:35.748
Some have found refuge in neighboring countries,

00:37:36.628 --> 00:37:37.630
as in Mauritania,

00:37:38.170 --> 00:37:39.672
the most stable state in the Sahel.

00:37:41.711 --> 00:37:44.934
The Mbera refugee camp is home to 67,000 people.

00:37:46.896 --> 00:37:50.637
Most of them are Tuaregs who fled jihadists in northern Mali in 2012.

00:37:51.458 --> 00:37:53.340
But the latest arrivals are all Fulani,

00:37:55.021 --> 00:37:55.722
like Birguisso.

00:37:56.521 --> 00:37:57.103
A year ago,

00:37:57.682 --> 00:37:59.563
This traditional chief fled his village,

00:38:00.125 --> 00:38:02.286
after being threatened by a Malian soldier.

00:38:04.106 --> 00:38:04.947
The soldier told me...

00:38:06.027 --> 00:38:07.668
I swear I won't tell you twice.

00:38:09.170 --> 00:38:10.550
I heard that the Fulani are killing us,

00:38:11.331 --> 00:38:12.512
that the jihadists kill us.

00:38:13.813 --> 00:38:14.413
And in this case,

00:38:14.992 --> 00:38:15.914
We will kill all the Fulani.

00:38:18.155 --> 00:38:21.876
So I called the sub-prefect of the jurisdiction and he told us not to move from our house.

00:38:22.577 --> 00:38:24.778
He told us that no one would hurt us.

00:38:26.860 --> 00:38:28.240
Despite these calls for help,

00:38:28.920 --> 00:38:31.521
no state authority takes Birguisso seriously.

00:38:33.023 --> 00:38:33.943
The following Friday.

00:38:34.820 --> 00:38:36.221
Soldiers came to the village.

00:38:38.081 --> 00:38:38.963
They surrounded him first.

00:38:40.063 --> 00:38:41.605
It was between 1 and 2 p.m.

00:38:42.764 --> 00:38:42.965
Then,

00:38:43.246 --> 00:38:44.326
They entered the village.

00:38:46.628 --> 00:38:48.068
They attacked everyone who was sitting.

00:38:49.030 --> 00:38:52.172
They entered the rooms and dragged the sick people out of their homes.

00:38:54.092 --> 00:38:55.114
They killed 7 people.

00:38:57.074 --> 00:38:58.615
The Fulani of the village are afraid.

00:38:59.079 --> 00:39:02.942
Birguiso then urgently organized the departure of 1,000 families to Mauritania.

00:39:03.882 --> 00:39:04.222
Today,

00:39:05.081 --> 00:39:05.782
where I am,

00:39:06.402 --> 00:39:06.963
we live in peace.

00:39:07.623 --> 00:39:08.284
I thank God.

00:39:09.684 --> 00:39:10.083
For now,

00:39:10.224 --> 00:39:11.324
even if we chartered a plane,

00:39:11.885 --> 00:39:12.666
I won't go back.

00:39:15.206 --> 00:39:17.768
What they did to us will remain etched in our memories.

00:39:18.387 --> 00:39:19.447
They murdered people.

00:39:21.708 --> 00:39:26.510
Birguiso and his villagers will not return to Mali until their safety is assured.

00:39:27.811 --> 00:39:28.211
Because here...

00:39:28.963 --> 00:39:31.105
In addition to United Nations food aid,

00:39:32.085 --> 00:39:35.628
Fulani refugees like him can resume an almost normal life,

00:39:36.427 --> 00:39:37.429
cultivate land,

00:39:37.889 --> 00:39:38.768
raise their animals,

00:39:42.871 --> 00:39:44.211
and even go to school,

00:39:45.572 --> 00:39:47.914
take care of the populations to gain their support.

00:39:48.635 --> 00:39:51.516
This is part of the overall strategy of the Mauritanian state.

00:39:53.757 --> 00:39:58.519
The country has also extensively restructured its army following around ten jihadist attacks.

00:39:58.943 --> 00:40:00.324
To the heart of the capital,

00:40:01.585 --> 00:40:04.668
Today it is considered the most professional in the region.

00:40:06.429 --> 00:40:09.793
One of the main air bases in Mauritania is located in Attar,

00:40:10.393 --> 00:40:11.414
at the gates of the Sahara.

00:40:13.014 --> 00:40:13.715
On the tarmac,

00:40:14.195 --> 00:40:16.318
devices that seem to come from another age,

00:40:17.119 --> 00:40:19.320
like this antique DC-3 from the 50s,

00:40:20.320 --> 00:40:22.463
or these Brazilian-made fighters.

00:40:23.784 --> 00:40:25.405
Despite their rudimentary appearance,

00:40:26.045 --> 00:40:28.507
They are perfectly suited to the war being waged here.

00:40:29.672 --> 00:40:32.375
Colonel Taleb is in charge of this squadron.

00:40:33.335 --> 00:40:34.155
This is the Super Tucano.

00:40:34.336 --> 00:40:38.179
This aircraft has double the range compared to the Tucano, with very powerful armament.

00:40:39.061 --> 00:40:43.525
And we have the ability to put different types of weaponry on it.

00:40:43.826 --> 00:40:46.047
We have two of these built-ins,

00:40:46.407 --> 00:40:49.371
electric machine guns and two rocket launchers.

00:40:50.612 --> 00:40:51.213
The AU-7A.

00:40:52.253 --> 00:40:54.175
You can put rockets in it. 70 mm.

00:40:55.244 --> 00:40:58.405
It's for vehicles, it's for vehicles.

00:40:59.065 --> 00:40:59.445
Often,

00:40:59.985 --> 00:41:02.565
The choice of weaponry depends on the target.

00:41:04.246 --> 00:41:10.047
These fighter jets have the advantage of being very maneuverable and can land on rough runways in the middle of the desert.

00:41:11.509 --> 00:41:12.969
But before you start hunting,

00:41:15.090 --> 00:41:17.409
The Mauritanian Air Force must uncover the menus.

00:41:18.951 --> 00:41:19.210
And that,

00:41:19.990 --> 00:41:22.010
This is the mission of reconnaissance aircraft.

00:41:26.313 --> 00:41:27.173
Permanently,

00:41:27.693 --> 00:41:33.697
These Cessna Caravans monitor the 2000 km of borders that Mauritania shares with its neighbor,

00:41:34.478 --> 00:41:34.898
Mali.

00:41:36.139 --> 00:41:36.679
In total,

00:41:37.239 --> 00:41:39.940
450,000 km² of desert,

00:41:41.041 --> 00:41:41.922
80%

00:41:41.922 --> 00:41:42.541
of France.

00:41:44.943 --> 00:41:47.505
Lieutenant Youssouf is a sensor operator.

00:41:48.565 --> 00:41:52.307
It controls the high-definition cameras that allow you to see up to 20 km.

00:42:06.653 --> 00:42:07.014
For them,

00:42:07.715 --> 00:42:10.036
Jihadists and traffickers are closely linked.

00:42:11.318 --> 00:42:11.798
This country,

00:42:12.338 --> 00:42:13.719
among the poorest in the world,

00:42:13.880 --> 00:42:15.242
did not skimp on the means.

00:42:16.163 --> 00:42:20.907
Each monitoring system costs a million dollars and allows the soil to be examined,

00:42:21.327 --> 00:42:22.507
in all circumstances.

00:42:33.847 --> 00:42:34.387
And above all,

00:42:35.188 --> 00:42:36.528
thanks to the thermal sensor,

00:42:37.250 --> 00:42:40.492
Lieutenant Youssouf sees the vehicle tracks in the sand,

00:42:41.492 --> 00:42:43.713
even several hours after their passage.

00:42:53.239 --> 00:42:55.141
Because the desert is not so empty.

00:42:55.981 --> 00:43:02.405
Nomads pitch their tents there and gold miners exploit the abundant gold in the region.

00:43:04.206 --> 00:43:04.427
Here,

00:43:05.228 --> 00:43:07.230
one of their trucks transporting equipment.

00:43:08.811 --> 00:43:09.811
If they spot any weapons,

